(In Tangkhul Naga, prefixal stop consonants exhibit systematic aspiration) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(dissimilation reminiscent of Grassmann's Law in Indo-European. When a) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(verbal root begins with an aspirated stop \(ph-, th-, kh-\), the preceding) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(nominalizing/infinitive prefix surfaces as an unaspirated stop [ke-].) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Conversely, when the verbal root begins with an unaspirated stop or) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(sonorant, the prefix is realized with robust aspiration [khe-] in) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(conservative varieties. Using acoustic measurements of Voice Onset Time) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(\(VOT\) and burst spectra from 8 native speakers, this paper confirms that) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
