0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Phonologists have long studied long-distance consonant interactions such) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(as consonant harmony and dissimilation. In Tangkhul, the interaction) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(between the prefix consonant and the root-initial consonant exhibits a) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(classic Obligatory Contour Principle \(OCP\) effect for the feature) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
([spread glottis]. Two adjacent syllables within the same phonological) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(stem cannot both surface with contrastive aspiration.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
